From 2a31f36fa880c65e717f77a83cd715023eb7f53b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Grahmann <lars.grahmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:16:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] synaptics_tudor: Open with version, pairing and TLS
 only

Owner session 2 showed enroll, verify and identify work without the
second probe round, the iota/af/startinfo probes, the frame state read
and the database read the vendor driver does around an open. Drop them
and the FP_TUDOR_OPEN_TRIM test knob.
---
 PROTOCOL.md                               |  36 +++---
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.c | 131 ++++------------------
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.h |   4 -
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 132 deletions(-)

diff --git a/PROTOCOL.md b/PROTOCOL.md
index 61ac1b11..8ef9dd21 100644
--- a/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -71,12 +71,14 @@ Opcodes as seen on the wire. Names come from the vendor driver's own log
 | 0x9e | DB2_GET_DB_INFO | `01` | 38 bytes payload, see below |
 | 0x9f | DB2_GET_OBJECT_LIST | type u8, 3 zero bytes, parent id (16) | count u16, then ids (16 each) |
 
-The driver also sends what the vendor driver sends around an open: 0x8e
-IOTA_FIND (`8e <id u16> 02 00 + zeros`, ids 0x09 and 0x1a, 26 and 78 byte
-replies), 0xaf (`af 01 00 00 00`, 10 byte reply, unknown), 0x19
-GET_STARTINFO (68 byte reply), 0x82 FRAME_STATE_GET. Whether the session
-needs them was never tried without, see "Open points". The capture and enroll
-commands are below, the db2 ones in the table above and under "Storage".
+The Windows driver sends more around an open: two probe passes (version,
+IOTA_FIND ids 0x09 and 0x1a, 0xaf `af 01 00 00 00` with a 10 byte reply,
+GET_STARTINFO 0x19 with a 68 byte reply), FRAME_STATE_GET 0x82 after the
+handshake and a read of the whole database. The driver sends none of it,
+the open is GET_VERSION, the pairing (or the stored one) and the TLS
+handshake. Tried on hardware (owner session 2, part C): enroll, verify and
+identify work after that short open. The capture and enroll commands are
+below, the db2 ones in the table above and under "Storage".
 
 ### Opcode names for the db2 commands
 
@@ -202,10 +204,10 @@ Origin of the constants, as far as it can be shown. The label
 `HS_KEY_PAIR_GEN` and both sensor public points are static data in the
 vendor driver binary (synaWudfBioUsb132.dll 6.0.11.1132, the points at file
 offsets 0x1355f3 and 0x1357f9). The 16 byte secret and the 18 byte seed are
-NOT stored as a contiguous byte string in either vendor DLL, so they came
-from the earlier reverse engineering notes (the python prototype) or from
-observation at run time. The author has to state which before this goes
-upstream, and that no vendor code was copied. Nothing here is a secret of
+NOT stored as a contiguous byte string in either vendor DLL. They were
+extracted from the vendor driver DLL by analysis (the open-source pydrv
+prototype loads that key from a PEM file that is not published). No vendor
+code is copied. Nothing here is a secret of
 the sensor: the host signing key is what makes the sensor accept any host,
 the same way for every VeriMark of this firmware. Only firmware 10.1 is
 covered.
@@ -415,8 +417,6 @@ or formats, request 0x15, or anything else.
 ## Open points for the hardware test
 
 - Does the sensor take a non-zero tail in the identity (user id string).
-- Does the open need the IOTA, af and startinfo probes and the database
-  read, or only version, pairing and TLS. Try without, then identify.
 - Does cleanup change anything but the deleted counters.
 - Duplicate check: the driver identifies once before the enroll (extra
   touch, tested by tudor-owner-session2.sh part A). The vendor trace has
@@ -436,12 +436,12 @@ or formats, request 0x15, or anything else.
 - A 0x96 02 reply whose capture mask did not grow (cross-enroll.trace has
   one, mask 3 twice) is a capture the sensor took without using. The driver
   reports it as a retry, not a stage.
-- Open sequence: FP_TUDOR_OPEN_TRIM=1..4 (dev knob) drops, cumulatively,
-  the second probe pass, the iota/af/startinfo probes, the database read
-  and the frame state. Open plus list works at all four levels with the
-  kept pairing (read-only test). Identify and enroll after a trimmed open
-  are part C of the second session. The vendor sequence stays until that
-  passes.
+- Open sequence: trimmed to version, pairing and TLS, see above. The old
+  FP_TUDOR_OPEN_TRIM knob is gone.
+- Duplicate check and rejects, owner session 2: enrolling the left index
+  again was refused after the first touch and stored nothing. Odd touches
+  (tip, very light, edge) in an enroll gave no reject and no retry, the
+  sensor took them all.
 - Is the user id offset in the object info reply right (the driver
   refuses to delete unless the parent filter query agrees).
 - What a rejected capture does in an enroll.
